meta {
  name: List My Agents (GET /v1/agents)
  type: http
  seq: 103
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/agents
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{sessionToken}}
}

vars:pre-request {
  baseUrl: http://localhost:8080
}

docs {
  # GET /v1/agents

  List the auth.md agent identities bound to the authenticated account — the wallet's "My agents"
  surface. Authenticate as the account owner with either a wallet session token or a full-access
  OAuth/XRPC access token; agent-derived and app-password credentials are refused (403).

  ## Response (200)

  ```json
  {
    "agents": [
      {
        "registrationId": "reg_...",
        "registrationType": "service_auth",
        "issuer": "https://idp.example",
        "subject": "agent-123",
        "scopes": ["repo:app.bsky.feed.post?action=create", "blob:image/*"],
        "effectiveScopes": ["repo:app.bsky.feed.post?action=create", "blob:image/*"],
        "status": "claimed",
        "createdAt": "2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z",
        "updatedAt": "2026-01-01T00:05:00.000Z",
        "lastUsedAt": "2026-01-02T12:00:00.000Z"
      },
      {
        "registrationId": "reg_...",
        "registrationType": "connector",
        "clientId": "https://mcp-client.example/oauth-client-metadata.json",
        "scopes": ["atproto", "transition:generic"],
        "effectiveScopes": ["atproto", "transition:generic"],
        "status": "claimed",
        "createdAt": "2026-01-03T00:00:00.000Z",
        "updatedAt": "2026-01-03T00:00:00.000Z",
        "lastUsedAt": "2026-01-03T00:15:00.000Z"
      }
    ],
    "scopeProfile": ["atproto", "blob:*/*", "repo:*?action=create&action=update"]
  }
  ```

  `scopeProfile` is the operator's current scope profile: the ceiling an owner can widen an agent
  to (`POST /v1/agents/{registration_id}/scopes`). `effectiveScopes` is the agent's grant clamped
  to it, what the agent holds now; a scope in `scopes` but not `effectiveScopes` is suspended. An
  OAuth grant isn't governed by the profile, so its `effectiveScopes` equals its `scopes`.

  `status` is `active` (registered, awaiting the claim ceremony), `claimed`, or `revoked`.
  `issuer`/`subject` appear only for `identity_assertion` registrations; `lastUsedAt` is the most
  recent token exchange / repo write / blob upload, absent for a never-used agent.
  `connector` (an MCP connector) and `oauth_app` (any other OAuth app) are OAuth grants: they carry
  `clientId`, start `claimed`, and drop off the list once every session of theirs has ended.
}
